title: Democracy Defense Program
subtitle: Lawyers, observers, and state-level coalitions.
tags: party_action
new-page: true
view-if: maga >= 15 or far_right >= 25
choose-if: funds >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: We need at least 3 funds.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; funds -= 3

= Democracy Defense Program

When the rules are contested, they must be defended before the contest, not after.

- @lawyers: Build a national election-protection bar.
- @states: Support state-level secretaries of state and election officials.
- @civic: Fund civic education and local news.
- @security: Quietly coordinate threat assessment with law enforcement.

@lawyers
subtitle: Litigation readiness.
on-arrival: stability += 5; media_trust += 1

Thousands of volunteer lawyers on call.

@states
subtitle: Bipartisan where possible.
on-arrival: stability += 4; far_right -= 2; maga -= 1

Local officials of both parties are the last line of defense.

@civic
subtitle: Slow, but it lasts.
on-arrival: stability += 2; media_trust += 4; far_left -= 1; far_right -= 1

A better-informed public is a more stable one.

@security
subtitle: Reduces extremist threat. Risks civil-liberties backlash.
on-arrival: far_right -= 6; far_left -= 3; stability += 2; prog_dissent += 3

Threat assessments are quiet work. They are also controversial.
